---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

// Changelog feed merged into this page (Aug 2026) — "where we're headed"
// and "what actually landed" belong next to each other. Pulls recently
// merged PRs from the public repos at build time via the GitHub REST API
// (unauthenticated — fine for a handful of requests per build, well
// under the 60/hr rate limit). Falls back to an empty list per-repo if a
// fetch fails (e.g. local dev with no network, or the repo is
// momentarily rate-limited) rather than failing the whole build.

const REPOS = [
  { repo: 'Chronophage-net/fates-edge-dev', label: 'Dev Portal' },
  { repo: 'Chronophage-net/fates-edge-apps', label: 'Apps' },
  { repo: 'Chronophage-net/fates-edge-ai-gm-bot', label: 'AI GM Bot' },
];

async function fetchMergedPRs({ repo, label }) {
  try {
    const url = `https://api.github.com/search/issues?q=repo:${repo}+is:pr+is:merged&sort=updated&order=desc&per_page=10`;
    const res = await fetch(url, {
      headers: { Accept: 'application/vnd.github+json' },
    });
    if (!res.ok) return [];
    const data = await res.json();
    return (data.items ?? []).map((item) => ({
      repo,
      label,
      title: item.title,
      number: item.number,
      url: item.html_url,
      mergedAt: item.closed_at,
      author: item.user?.login,
    }));
  } catch {
    return [];
  }
}

const results = await Promise.all(REPOS.map(fetchMergedPRs));
const entries = results
  .flat()
  .filter((e) => e.mergedAt)
  .sort((a, b) => new Date(b.mergedAt) - new Date(a.mergedAt))
  .slice(0, 30);

function fmtDate(iso) {
  return new Date(iso).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'short', day: 'numeric' });
}
---
<DocsLayout title="Roadmap & Changelog" description="Where Fate's Edge is headed, and a rolling feed of what's actually landed.">
  <h1>Roadmap</h1>
  <p>A living, lightweight view of where Fate's Edge is headed — not a promise of dates. The authoritative, granular backlog lives in each repo's issue tracker; this page is the "why would I care" summary for new contributors. For what's already shipped, jump to the <a href="#changelog">Changelog</a> below.</p>
  <p>Bigger milestones get a proper write-up on the <a href="https://blog.fates-edge.com">dev blog</a> when they land — this page just tracks direction.</p>

  <h2>Now</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Stabilizing the Tag DSL surface so third-party GM directives don't break on upgrade.</li>
    <li>Expanding transport-layer event parity across all client surfaces.</li>
    <li>Growing the LLM driver roster beyond the current defaults.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Next</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A mobile-friendly client surface.</li>
    <li>More adventure modules from the community, using the JSON-based, rules-native format.</li>
    <li>Voice stack adapters beyond the current TTS/RVC pipeline.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Later / exploratory</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Additional VTT integrations beyond Roll20 and Foundry.</li>
    <li>Community-run adventure module registry.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The content track</h2>
  <p>The lists above are software. A comparable amount of work happens on the books, and it has its own backlog — worth stating, because some of it is more approachable than the code for anyone who'd rather write or proofread than commit.</p>
  <p><strong>Where it stands:</strong> 64 documents published to the reader — the SRD, both guides, 24 adventures, 21 expansions, 6 anthology volumes and the quickstarts — against roughly 114 LaTeX sources in the repository. So a meaningful fraction of the writing exists only as <code>.tex</code> and isn't readable by anyone who hasn't cloned it.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Regenerate the LaTeX from the HTML.</strong> The pipeline currently points the wrong way. The repo was built as LaTeX-to-everything, but the HTML is what gets published and therefore what gets corrected, so the <code>.tex</code> sources have drifted — several still carry a retired Threat Level table, the previous edition's skill names and the old Position-overflow rule. The fix is to generate the LaTeX <em>from</em> the corrected HTML rather than merge two divergent copies by hand. Blocked first on the Player's Guide not compiling at all (missing <code>fontawesome5.sty</code>).</li>
    <li><strong>Convert the remaining supplements.</strong> Roughly forty LaTeX-only files, triaged in the repo's <code>GUIDES_TODO.md</code>: a handful worth converting as they stand, a larger group that should be absorbed into documents that already exist rather than shipped as thin separate books, and one that's simply misfiled.</li>
    <li><strong>A fourth Peoples and Cultures volume.</strong> Twelve cultures still have no write-up — Ecktoria, Vhasia, Kahfagia, Silkstrand, Ashaan, Dhahara, Ubral, Fhara, Oshiira, Trow, Hag/Morag and the Linn. The source material for these is thin, so this one is authoring rather than conversion.</li>
    <li><strong>The canonical-skill sweep.</strong> Every roll, prerequisite and NPC block in the Player's Guide checked against the sixteen skills. Tedious, mechanical, and exactly the kind of thing that's easy to review a PR for.</li>
    <li><strong>Two manifest generators disagree.</strong> <code>sync_data_to_consumers.py</code> and <code>generate-manifests.js</code> emit different bytes for the same file, so the apps tree flaps on every sync. Small, self-contained, and annoying to whoever touches it next.</li>
    <li><strong>A character migration tool.</strong> The skill list consolidated from sixteen to twelve, and the web client folds retired skills into their successors on load. That covers characters in the app; it does not cover a sheet somebody wrote out by hand, a PDF export, or a third-party tool. A small standalone converter &mdash; paste a character, get the twelve-skill version back &mdash; would close that, and is a contained first contribution.</li>
    <li><strong>Heritage isn't applied by the dice roller.</strong> <code>roller.js</code> clamps Position correctly but doesn't read a character's Affinity or Limit, so players apply it by hand. A contained web-client task.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Want to influence this list? Open an issue on the relevant repo, or raise it in <a href="https://github.com/Chronophage-net/fates-edge-dev/discussions">Discussions</a> or the <a href="https://discord.gg/etmb7DYbj">Discord</a> — roadmap items generally start there before they're formalized.</p>

  <hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin: 3rem 0;" />

  <h1 id="changelog">Changelog</h1>
  <p>A rolling feed of what's actually landed, pulled straight from merged pull requests across the public repos. For the running commentary on why something was built a certain way, see the <a href="https://blog.fates-edge.com">dev blog</a>.</p>

  {entries.length === 0 && (
    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Couldn't reach GitHub at build time.</strong> This section pulls live data during the site build — try a rebuild, or see each repo's Pull Requests tab directly in the meantime.
    </div>
  )}

  <ul class="changelog-list">
    {entries.map((e) => (
      <li>
        <span class="changelog-date">{fmtDate(e.mergedAt)}</span>
        <span class="changelog-repo">{e.label}</span>
        <a href={e.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{e.title}</a>
        <span class="changelog-meta">#{e.number}{e.author ? ` · ${e.author}` : ''}</span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .changelog-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.9rem;
  }
  .changelog-list li {
    padding-bottom: 0.9rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.5rem 0.6rem;
  }
  .changelog-date {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, monospace);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text3);
    min-width: 6.5rem;
  }
  .changelog-repo {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--gold);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    background: rgba(201,168,76,0.1);
    padding: 0.1rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .changelog-list a {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
  }
  .changelog-meta {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text3);
  }
</style>
